WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.930
In a small, sleepy Oregon town, Jacob Pierce
was turning 10 years old.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:10.309
His friends and family had gathered for a
birthday party in their local park.

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:14.900
It had all the makings of a perfect day for
a young boy entering the double digits for

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.330
the first time.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:20.539
There was a hired magician attempting to make
balloon animals as children loudly mocked

00:00:20.539 --> 00:00:21.539
him.

00:00:21.539 --> 00:00:25.330
There was cake, ice cream, and an ice cream
cake for those who couldn’t make up their

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.349
mind about which they’d rather have.

00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:32.470
There were pizzas, pepperoni and cheese, and
bowl after bowl of chips.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:35.380
Jacob was having the best day ever.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:39.809
As he blew out the candles on his birthday
cake, he quietly wished for something amazing

00:00:39.809 --> 00:00:40.850
to happen.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:44.590
It was already a good day, but it was also
a little bit mundane.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:50.739
A fan of science fiction and fantasy, Jacob
had always quietly hoped that turning 10 would

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:53.680
usher in an era of magic and mystery.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.580
Perhaps he would encounter aliens for the
first time.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:01.410
Maybe he would solve a grand mystery or learn
about a civilization of tiny people living

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.840
in his backyard.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:08.650
Or maybe, just maybe, he would wake up to
find he had acquired magical powers.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:13.160
Suddenly, he would cease to be an ordinary
young boy who had to worry about math homework

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.720
and playground bullies.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:19.590
He would instead become something special,
someone who could change the world around

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:25.000
him and finally make a difference, just like
the heroes of all of his favorite books.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.939
So, as his mother set the cake down in front
of him and everyone sang “Happy Birthday”

00:01:29.939 --> 00:01:34.710
with loud, off-key enthusiasm, Jacob closed
his eyes and wished.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:38.220
Little did he know that his wish was about
to come true.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.940
At least, it sort of was.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:45.310
After cake, it was time for every kid’s
favorite part of their birthday party: the

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:46.310
presents.

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:51.680
A stack of colorfully wrapped packages sat
on the picnic table, just waiting to be unwrapped.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.869
Jacob bounced excitedly, waiting for his mother
to give the all-clear.

00:01:55.869 --> 00:02:00.810
She gathered all the kids, and Jacob’s nineteen-year-old
brother Nathan, and instructed them to sit

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:03.220
down and watch Jacob open his gifts.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:08.110
He tore the paper from board games, action
figures, and an ill-advised stuffed animal

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:12.770
or two, when suddenly Nathan produced a package
he hadn’t seen before.

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:15.690
It was a small lumpy item, wrapped in green
paper.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:20.120
He handed it to Jacob, who, thrilled to be
receiving a special present from his beloved

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.660
older brother, immediately opened it.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:27.440
There, was a toy dart gun, already loaded
with a large foam dart.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.360
Overcome with excitement, Jacob jumped up
from his seat and asked if he could play with

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:32.360
it now.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:36.220
His mother said it was fine, and Jacob and
his friends immediately jumped into action.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:41.200
They ran across the park, as Jacob aimed the
dart gun and decided which target to fire

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.200
it at.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:46.060
As he squeezed the trigger, aiming for his
best friend Trevor, Nathan called out to him.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.350
“Don’t shoot it at him!”

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:49.400
He yelled, with sudden urgency.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:53.970
Startled, Jacob moved at the last minute,
and the dart fired at a nearby stone wall

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:56.940
instead of its original nine-year-old target.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:02.150
As soon as the dart hit the wall, it transformed
into a wobbly stack of large stones.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:06.070
The stones tumbled down, landing on several
people standing nearby.

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:09.990
A man who had been leaning on the wall fell
to the ground, where his leg was crushed under

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:11.310
a falling stone.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:15.310
The magician, who was packing up his supplies,
took a rock to the head and was immediately

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:16.970
knocked unconscious.

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:21.700
The park broke into pandemonium, people running
and screaming, trying to figure out how a

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:25.290
previously solid wall had turned into falling
rocks.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:30.260
Nathan scooped up Jacob, the gun, and the
dart and pulled him away from the chaos.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:34.290
Someone called the police, where an embedded
SCP Foundation operative was alerted to the

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.920
situation unfolding.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:40.950
Before Jacob and his family could vacate the
park, two SCP operatives were already arriving

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.180
on the scene.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:46.090
After speaking with several eyewitnesses,
they identified the source of the anomalous

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:50.540
activity as the toy gun, and seized it for
further investigation.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:55.260
All witnesses, including Jacob and his mother,
were given amnestics in order to erase their

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:58.290
memory of the toy gun and the incident in
the park.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:01.930
Nathan Pierce, who was considered a person
of interest for his initial possession of

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:03.780
the gun could not be found.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:08.350
He fled detection and Foundation custody,
further indicating his knowledge of the gun’s

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:13.350
anomalous properties, and possibly indicating
he was responsible for its creation.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:18.600
His online activity linked him to an organization
satirically called Gamers Against Weed, a

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:23.250
Group of Interest that had previously been
linked to other anomalies seized by the Foundation.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:28.070
His younger brother Jacob had, without any
knowledge, received a birthday gift that would

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:31.190
become designated SCP-3108.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:37.840
SCP-3108 is a modified Nerf brand dart gun
that, when paired with its foam dart ammunition

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:44.110
- designated SCP-3108-1 - demonstrates anomalous
transformative properties.

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:49.180
When it fires other Nerf darts, it behaves
like an ordinary toy, and the same goes for

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.690
the dart when fired from any other Nerf gun.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:57.720
The only notable difference between SCP-3108
and any other ordinary toy dart gun is the

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:02.460
writing on the side, which reads “OP PLS
NERF” in red ink.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:08.130
When SCP-3108 is fired at an object, it will
immediately be transformed or altered in a

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:11.650
way that turns it into a worse version of
itself.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:15.930
This can range anywhere from small changes
to complete transformation on a molecular

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:16.930
scale.

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:20.600
The law of conservation of mass does not apply
to these changes, and the gun’s effects

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:23.090
appear to defy the laws of physics.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:27.480
The transformed objects are not themselves
anomalous in any way, and the changes they

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:32.920
undergo appear to be influenced, not by objective
reality, but by the opinion of whoever wields

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:33.950
the gun.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:39.460
Whatever the person firing SCP-3108 thinks
would make the target worse, is what comes

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:40.670
to pass.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:46.500
An external examination of SCP-3108 revealed
that it is made of a steel outer shell, with

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.530
decorative bronze inlays.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:53.020
It can be physically damaged but resists any
attempts to take it apart.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:56.770
Security Officer Silva attempted to take it
apart with his hands during a round of tests,

00:05:56.770 --> 00:06:01.340
but before he could break open the shell he
found his hands had transformed into a pair

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.860
of rubber gloves.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:08.330
They hung, limp and useless from his wrists
as he flopped them around yelling for assistance.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:13.060
Officer Silva was promptly placed on leave,
and no more attempts to disassemble SCP-3108

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:15.240
have been made since.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:21.050
Aside from this one instance, SCP-3108 does
not have an effect on objects that are not

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:22.690
directly hit by its dart.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:27.830
A variety of tests were performed, headed
by Dr. Johnson and Dr. Dietz, in order to

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:31.050
further examine the anomalous properties of
SCP-3108.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:37.180
First, a traditional dart board made of sisal
fibers was set up on the wall of the lab.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:43.510
When hit with SCP-3108-1, the dart board changed
to a cork board of the same shape and size,

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:47.030
filled with several small holes and bearing
a noticeable beer stain.

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:51.590
A piece of eight by eleven printer paper was
transformed into a square of single-ply toilet

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:52.590
paper.

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:56.830
A sturdy coffee mug from the on-site cafeteria
changed into a small tea cup made of the same

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:58.020
kind of ceramic.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:02.950
A dollar changed into a fake one hundred dollar
bill from the board game Monopoly.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:06.430
It was determined that the gun’s effects
are determined by the personal preference

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:09.460
of the person firing it when it was fired
at a can of Coke.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:14.580
The can immediately turned into a can of Pepsi,
much to the dismay of Security Officer Mike

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.370
who was observing the experiment and who preferred
Pepsi.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:22.590
He took the gun next, and fired it at the
can, which promptly turned back into Coke.

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:28.010
On another day of trials, a VHS tape of the
1971 film Willy Wonka and the Chocolate Factory

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:33.370
was transformed into a DVD copy of the 2005
remake of the same film, prompting the research

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:36.740
team to wonder: Does the gun have a sense
of humor?

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:37.740
It seemed to.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:41.550
Next, the research team began conducting trials
on living organisms.

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:45.449
A rat was transformed into an ant, which Dr.
Dietz found confusing.

00:07:45.449 --> 00:07:50.250
A female Golden Retriever was turned into
a female American Shorthair cat, unusually

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:56.790
large at a weight of 15.4 kilograms, and displaying
behavior more consistent with that of a dog.

00:07:56.790 --> 00:08:01.000
After rats and dogs, the team decided to move
forward into human trials.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:05.340
A 28-year-old male was hit with the gun, and
promptly turned into a living specimen of

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:07.450
Homo Neanderthalensis.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:12.340
Right before the research team’s eyes, he
regressed into a real, live Neanderthal.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:16.200
After this trial, the team decided to see
how dangerous the gun could be if pushed to

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:17.639
the limits.

00:08:17.639 --> 00:08:23.320
Security Officer Gardiner was handed SCP-3108
and ordered to fire the gun repeatedly, reloading

00:08:23.320 --> 00:08:25.810
each time, until told to stop.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:30.180
A 24-year-old man was instructed to stand
in firing range and remain still.

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:32.770
First, he transformed into a prehistoric man.

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:37.829
Then, an unidentified species of gibbon,
and next, a three-toed sloth.

00:08:37.829 --> 00:08:42.960
On nine occasions of the gun being fired,
the subject did not change species but rather

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:46.300
took on physical signs of injury or disease.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:51.310
After 46 shots, testing was finally stopped
after the subject was reduced to a small variety

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:52.880
of earthworm.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:57.560
After attempting to track him down unsuccessfully
for months, Nathan Pierce was finally located

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:02.690
by Foundation personnel and apprehended at
an Internet café in Los Angeles, California.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:08.550
He was taken into custody and brought to Site-64
for questioning about the creation of SCP-3108.

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:13.120
Dr. Dietz conducted the interview, and asked
why Nathan created the gun.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:17.060
Nathan referred to it as “the Nerfing gun,”
and explained that he thought it would be

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:18.060
funny.

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:21.950
It didn’t have any particularly grand purpose
or intention, it was just something he had

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:24.460
come up with and thought would be entertaining.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:28.260
He experimented with it for a while, got bored
of it, and then gave it to his brother as

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:29.260
a gift.

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:33.730
His only regret was not giving his brother
a proper warning on how to use it before doing

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:34.730
so.

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:38.830
Dr. Dietz applied a little pressure, insisting
that the anomaly was dangerous and could turn

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:40.470
“people into invertebrates.”

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:44.610
This stopped the interview cold, as Nathan
became visibly distressed.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:48.930
He insisted that it was never intended to
be used on people, but for low-level mischief.

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:53.790
He concluded the interview by saying, “Why
would you turn a joke into a torture device?”

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:57.630
and demanded that Dr. Dietz leave his cell
and stop speaking to him.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:02.750
Nathan Pierce was later released from custody,
and the containment procedures for SCP-3108

00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:05.910
were updated with this new information in
mind.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:11.490
SCP-3108 is contained in a standard anomalous
object containment vault in Site-64 and is

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:15.450
not allowed to be removed from said vault
except for use in experiments.

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:20.110
Proposed testing must be approved by Dr. Johnson
and Dr. Dietz before it can be conducted.

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:25.040
The gun may not be stored while loaded, and
the foam dart is stored in a separate containment

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:26.080
vault.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:33.380
During any and all testing, SCP-3108 is only
to be handled by Site-64 security staff.

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:38.050
Only one officer may hold and fire the object
at a time, while a secondary officer observes

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:42.510
and watches for potential accidents or any
unapproved use of the item.

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:46.550
Researchers and D-class personnel are not
permitted to fire the gun, due to concerns

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:48.390
about safety and security.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:53.330
It may not be used, under any circumstances,
in cross-testing with other SCP objects.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:58.180
It is also forbidden from use in any testing
on humanoids, as this is now considered an

00:10:58.180 --> 00:10:59.750
ethics violation.

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:03.570
How would you use The Nerfing Gun if ever
it fell into your hands, and what do you think

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:04.570
would happen?

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:08.960
Let us know down in the comments, or we’ll
shoot, and make your comments terrible.

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:14.610
Now go check out “Irresistible Pick-up Artist
SCP-3512 - The More You Know” and “Top

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:19.250
8 SCP Objects You Actually Want” for more
dark and often hilarious anomalies!

